---
/**
 * The rotary kiln takes limestone and clay through 1,450°, where the lime,
 * silica and alumina stop sitting together and react into calcium silicates that
 * partly melt and fuse into clinker. Ground fine and wetted, those silicates
 * take water into their crystal structure and grow interlocking needles. It is a
 * reaction with water, not a drying — which is why concrete cures sealed, cures
 * under the sea, and gets hot doing it.
 */
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 960 440" role="img" aria-label="A rotary kiln taking the charge to clinker at 1,450 degrees, and calcium silicate needles interlocking as they hydrate">
  <defs>
    <marker id="pc-ar" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
      <path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" class="dg-ink" />
    </marker>
    <marker id="pc-ar-a" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
      <path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" class="dg-accent" />
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <text class="dg-lbl" x="30" y="24">ROTARY KILN · THE CHARGE RUNS DOWNHILL AS IT HEATS</text>

  <!-- the kiln, sloping -->
  <path class="dg-panel" d="M70 92 L470 168 V218 L70 142 Z" />
  <path class="dg-s" d="M70 92 L470 168 V218 L70 142 Z" />
  <path class="dg-m" d="M70 106 L470 182" />

  <!-- charge tumbling down the barrel -->
  <g class="dg-m">
    <path d="M108 128 h18 v8 h-18 Z M158 138 h18 v8 h-18 Z M208 147 h18 v8 h-18 Z" />
  </g>
  <g class="dg-ink">
    <path d="M290 165 h16 v9 h-16 Z M340 175 h16 v9 h-16 Z M392 184 h16 v9 h-16 Z" />
  </g>

  <!-- feed in at the high end -->
  <path class="dg-a" d="M50 66 L66 100" marker-end="url(#pc-ar-a)" />
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-key" x="30" y="58">LIMESTONE AND CLAY IN</text>

  <!-- burner at the low end -->
  <path class="dg-accent" d="M470 178 C500 178, 520 186, 534 196 C520 206, 500 214, 470 214 Z" />
  <path class="dg-s" d="M534 190 H580" />
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="588" y="196">BURNER</text>

  <!-- rollers -->
  <circle cx="176" cy="158" r="12" class="dg-m" />
  <circle cx="360" cy="197" r="12" class="dg-m" />
  <path class="dg-s" d="M156 176 H196 M340 215 H380" />

  <!-- the temperature gradient along the barrel -->
  <path class="dg-m" d="M70 250 H470" />
  <path class="dg-m" d="M70 244 V256 M470 244 V256" />
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="70" y="272">DRYING, ~100°</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="250" y="272" text-anchor="middle">CALCINING, ~900°</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-key" x="470" y="272" text-anchor="end">CLINKERING, 1,450°</text>

  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="30" y="308">ABOVE 1,450° THE LIME, SILICA AND ALUMINA STOP MERELY SITTING</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="30" y="322">TOGETHER AND REACT INTO CALCIUM SILICATES, WHICH PARTLY MELT</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="30" y="336">AND FUSE INTO CLINKER.</text>

  <!-- clinker out, ground -->
  <path class="dg-a" d="M508 220 L520 252" marker-end="url(#pc-ar-a)" />
  <g class="dg-ink">
    <path d="M496 262 h14 v9 h-14 Z M516 268 h12 v8 h-12 Z M534 260 h13 v9 h-13 Z" />
  </g>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-key" x="496" y="292">CLINKER, GROUND</text>

  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="30" y="368">SHAPE BECOMES CHEAP: A STONE STRUCTURE IS LIMITED TO WHAT A MASON</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="30" y="382">CAN CUT AND LIFT, WHILE CONCRETE TAKES THE SHAPE OF WHATEVER MOULD</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="30" y="396">CAN BE BUILT FROM TIMBER, AT THE SCALE OF A DAM.</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="30" y="418">WHAT IT CANNOT DO IS STRETCH — ABOUT A TENTH AS MUCH TENSION AS</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="30" y="432">COMPRESSION — SO IT NEEDS STEEL BARS INSIDE IT TO BECOME A SYSTEM.</text>

  <!-- ══ hydration ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <path class="dg-m" d="M620 14 V430" />
  <text class="dg-lbl" x="648" y="24">HYDRATION · A REACTION, NOT A DRYING</text>

  <!-- before: ground grains in water -->
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="648" y="56">MIXED</text>
  <rect x="648" y="66" width="128" height="110" class="dg-tint" />
  <rect x="648" y="66" width="128" height="110" class="dg-h" />
  <g class="dg-m">
    <path d="M668 92 h16 v12 h-16 Z M706 84 h14 v12 h-14 Z M740 100 h15 v11 h-15 Z
             M662 132 h15 v11 h-15 Z M700 140 h16 v12 h-16 Z M736 128 h14 v12 h-14 Z" />
  </g>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="648" y="194">GRAINS IN WATER</text>

  <path class="dg-m" d="M790 120 H812" marker-end="url(#pc-ar)" />

  <!-- after: needles interlocking -->
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="826" y="56">SET</text>
  <rect x="826" y="66" width="104" height="110" class="dg-page" />
  <rect x="826" y="66" width="104" height="110" class="dg-h" />
  <g class="dg-a">
    <path d="M844 88 L878 108 M878 76 L850 116 M896 82 L866 122 M842 130 L884 142
             M900 118 L864 150 M912 92 L880 130 M836 106 L872 96 M888 152 L916 128
             M852 156 L896 138 M838 148 L866 166" />
  </g>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-key" x="826" y="194">NEEDLES INTERLOCK</text>

  <path class="dg-m" d="M648 216 H930" />
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="648" y="240">THE SILICATES TAKE WATER INTO THEIR CRYSTAL</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="648" y="254">STRUCTURE. THAT IS WHY CONCRETE:</text>

  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="668" y="286">CURES IN A SEALED FORM,</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="668" y="306">CURES UNDER THE SEA,</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="668" y="326">AND GETS HOTTER WHILE IT DOES IT.</text>
  <path class="dg-m" d="M652 282 H660 M652 302 H660 M652 322 H660" />

  <text class="dg-lbl dg-key" x="648" y="360">A LARGE POUR HAS TO BE COOLED.</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="648" y="392">PATENT 1824 · THE NAME COMES FROM THE STONE</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="648" y="406">OF PORTLAND, WHICH THE SET CEMENT RESEMBLES.</text>
</svg>
